onempty. Then the function $v_{\\mathcal{X}$ is submodular if and only if there exists a unique minimal $\\mathcal{X}$-matroid.\nL20: — 【9†Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties】  (2502.00799 - Liwski et al., 2 Feb 2025) in Section 6, \\\"Connections to \\(\\mathcal{X}\\)-matroids\\), Conjecture following Lemma 6.4\nL21: ### Related Problems\nL22: \nL23: 1.\nL24: \nL25: 【10†Algorithm for identifying minimal X-matroids】  【11†Same Paper】\nL26: \nL27: 2.\nL28: \nL29: 【12†General containment criterion for realizable matroid varieties】  【11†Same Paper】\nL30: \nL31: 3.\nL32: \nL33: 【13†One-component conjecture for minimal non-Euclidean matroids】  【14†2501.12951】\nL34: \nL35: 4.\nL36: \nL37: 【15†Modular-cut subextension existence】  【14†2501.12951】\nL38: \nL39: 5.\nL40: \nL41: 【16†Structure of minimal thick matroids】  【17†2502.08945】\nL42: \nL43: 6.\nL44: \nL45: 【18†Extremality of direct sums】  【19†2502.20157】\nL46: \nL47: 7.\nL48: 【20†Maximal tensor products of uniform matroids and birigidity duality】  【21†2508.11636】\nL49: \nL50: 8.\nL51: \nL52: 【22†Ultra-generalized basis exchange conjecture】  【23†2511.16021】\nL53: \nL54: 9.\nL55: \nL56: 【24†Graver’s maximality conjecture for d = 3】  【21†2508.11636】\nL57: \nL58: 10.\nL59: \nL60: 【25†Extreme points of graphing cycle-matroid base polytopes】  【26†2608.16464】\nL61: \nL62: Content\nL63: \nL64: 【27†Statement】 【28†Background】 【29†References】 【30†Related Problems】\nL65: 【31†About】 【32†Whiteboards】 【33†Videos】 【34†Labs】 【35†Email Digest】 【7†Chrome Extension†chromewebstore.google.com】 【36†RSS】 【37†Terms】 【38†Privacy】 【39†Contact】 【40†Twitter†twitter.com】 【41†Discord†discord.gg】 【42†YouTube†www.youtube.com】\n"
